  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda: Enhancing Skills and Enabling Financial Inclusion for Young Women in the Creative Economy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Program&amp;nbsp;&amp;ldquo;Enhancing Skills and Enabling Financial Inclusion for Young Women in the Creative Economy&amp;rdquo;&amp;nbsp;is a 3-year initiative that supports 84,000 young women in Uganda, directly enabling 40,000 to access dignified work. Aligned with the Young Africa Works strategy and Uganda&amp;rsquo;s 2030 vision, it addresses barriers such as limited finance, skills gaps, and negative societal attitudes. The program focuses on three pillars: (1)&amp;nbsp;skills and talent development, equipping young women with practical, digital, entrepreneurial, and financial skills while linking them to creative markets; (2)&amp;nbsp;entrepreneurial support, growing young women-led MSMEs through incubation, business literacy, and digital entrepreneurship; and (3)&amp;nbsp;inclusive finance, piloting tailored products for MSMEs. Implemented by ITC, Bayimba, NextCom, and other partners, the program leverages Uganda&amp;rsquo;s vibrant creative and cultural industries to expand youth employment, strengthen financial inclusion, and transform perceptions of youth and women in the creative economy.</narrative>
  </description>
